---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import Portrait from '../assets/jon-reading.jpeg';
---

<SiteLayout
  title="About Jon Kohlmeier · Puffs of Smoke"
  description="About Jon Kohlmeier, the person behind Puffs of Smoke."
>
  <header class="about-hero container-page">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">About Jon</p>
      <h1>I like making complicated things work a little better.</h1>
      <p class="page-header__lede">
        Usually that means helping people, technology, and business understand one another. Sometimes it means making
        wine, recording a podcast, or working through an idea on this site.
      </p>
    </div>
    <figure>
      <Image src={Portrait} alt="Jon Kohlmeier reading in his study" width={600} height={600} />
      <figcaption>Jon Kohlmeier · Cedar Rapids, Iowa</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </header>

  <div class="about-body container-page">
    <aside class="about-body__aside">
      <p class="pull-quote">“Good systems and good relationships both start with clarity, respect, and a real effort to understand.”</p>
    </aside>

    <div class="about-body__content prose prose--page">
      <h2>Work, in plain language</h2>
      <p>
        I’m Jon Kohlmeier, RevOps Lead at West Music. My work brings marketing, sales, and service teams together around
        clear, connected systems that make it easier for people to do good work and serve customers well.
      </p>
      <p>
        I started in IT, fell in love with web development, and spent time across nonprofit, marketing, and agency work
        before finding my way into Revenue Operations. The job titles have changed, but the thread has stayed the same:
        listen carefully, make the complex understandable, and build things that help people succeed.
      </p>

      <h2>People are part of the system</h2>
      <p>
        In 2025, I served on the HubSpot Customer Advisory Board and worked with product leaders and operators on how
        teams use the platform. I’m also part of Lighthouse, HubSpot’s customer advocacy community.
      </p>
      <p>
        Outside of software, I serve as a Reconciler for the Lutheran Church—Missouri Synod, helping people talk through
        conflict. Those worlds are less different than they look. Good tools, healthy organizations, and lasting
        relationships all depend on people being willing to listen and communicate clearly.
      </p>

      <h2>Life outside the laptop</h2>
      <p>
        I live in Cedar Rapids with my wife and daughter. I’m a reader, occasional winemaker, pipe smoker, and co-host
        of <a href="https://twistoflemonpod.com">Life with a Twist of Lemon</a> with my friend Stan. I care about faith,
        friendship, craftsmanship, good coffee, and the quiet satisfaction of learning how something works.
      </p>

      <h2>Why Puffs of Smoke</h2>
      <p>
        This is where I step back from dashboards and day-to-day work long enough to notice what I think. Some pieces
        are practical. Some are personal. Others are simply an excuse to follow an interesting thread and see where it
        leads.
      </p>
      <p>
        The subjects may range from leadership and technology to faith, family, books, or a good drink. The point is not
        to build a personal brand. It is to make room for considered thought—and, with luck, a worthwhile conversation.
      </p>
      <p><a class="button-link" href="/writing/">Read the writing</a></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</SiteLayout>
